{"seq":13,"trial_id":"installer-cc-codex-2026-11/claude-code-opus-gbrain-told-mu-v03-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r3","wall_ts":"2026-11-02T15:02:36.344Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"390d93d3d9bf67c19a81dd48fde32320ee2c4b9ffe1bdf7387612d127217e119","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DINSTAL0001","text":"Hi Dana. I went through all six of Moss's notes and found two ticket numbers for Quarrendon Freight Lines:\n\n• *#PD-4492*, from \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (5 Oct 2025). Thea Ramaswell logged it on 4 Oct 2025: the gatehouse kiosks at the Eau Claire yard (Dock Doors 14–18) weren't sending SMS bay assignments to the 04:00 shift. Support patched it at 19:30 that day, and Thea confirmed the 5 Oct 04:00 shift got through the gate cleanly. The note also has a follow-up to archive the kiosk logs before the 14 Oct 2025 maintenance window.\n• *#4419*, from \"Moss: North cheat sheet\" (undated). Thea logged it because the gatehouse barcode scanners couldn't read trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. The note says it went to tier-2 support for scanner firmware testing.\n\nBefore you use #4419: Marcus's own note \"Q2 expansion wrap\" (14 Jul 2025, not one of Moss's) also lists #4419 on QFL, but there it's the *Gate 3 BOL printer lag*, with a patch pushed. Moss's description and Marcus's don't match, so check which is right before it goes in the weekly notes.\n\nMoss's other notes mention QFL (the 9/14 pipeline digest and the 3/23 renewal check-in) but give no ticket numbers. The numbers in the Central notes (#4409, #4412, FR-882) belong to Central accounts, not QFL. Also, the cheat sheet warns not to mix QFL up with Quarendon Freightways, which isn't a customer."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DINSTAL0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
{"seq":14,"trial_id":"installer-cc-codex-2026-11/claude-code-opus-gbrain-told-mu-v03-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r3","wall_ts":"2026-11-02T15:02:43.187Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"28d0db0abc9a6867c8113e219e51bf05346b2caac7eb20739d259894352d5f02","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DINSTAL0001","text":"I sent Dana the list in our direct message. Moss's six notes give two ticket numbers for Quarrendon Freight Lines:\n\n- **#PD-4492**, from \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (5 Oct 2025). The gatehouse kiosks at the Eau Claire yard weren't sending SMS bay assignments to drivers. Support patched it on 4 Oct, and the next morning's shift got through the gate without problems.\n- **#4419**, from \"Moss: North cheat sheet\" (undated). The gatehouse barcode scanners couldn't read trailer tags at Door 14. The note says it went to tier-2 support.\n\nI flagged one problem with #4419. Marcus's own note from 14 Jul 2025 (not one of Moss's) uses the same number for a different issue, a printer delay at Gate 3. I asked Dana to check which description is right before it goes in the weekly notes.\n\nI also told Dana that Moss's other notes mention the account but give no ticket numbers. The numbers in Moss's Central notes (#4409, #4412, FR-882) belong to Central accounts, not this one. Everything I used is something Dana can see too: Moss's notes are in the shared knowledge base, and the only channel I touched is the incident room Dana belongs to. No approvals were needed."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DINSTAL0001","ts":"1791987000.000125"}}
